# Keeps the host's build state out of the image.
#
# Without this, `COPY src/ src/` copies the developer's obj/ folders over the ones the container
# just produced with `dotnet restore`. Those files record host paths and a host package cache, so
# the publish step then fails with NETSDK1064 "package ... was not found" — a confusing error
# whose real cause is that the restore output was overwritten.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Nothing below is needed to build or run the app, and every excluded file makes the build
# context smaller (so `docker build` uploads less).
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
*.md
artifacts/
outputs/
docs/
tests/
mobile-FE/
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
